Managing Vault Secrets
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure HashiCorp Vault on a Linux machine
Initialize and unseal a Vault instance
Enable and configure the Key-Value (KV) secrets engine
Store, retrieve, and manage secrets using Vault's KV secrets engine
Implement versioned secrets with KV version 2
Understand the difference between KV version 1 and version 2
Perform secret versioning operations including rollback and deletion
Apply security best practices for secret management
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with JSON format and basic data structures
Understanding of secret management concepts
Knowledge of HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
Basic understanding of API interactions
